[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  everyone must live with their own minor  handicap I for instance cannot see more  than a vague blur without my glasses on  Peter Brown has to contend with a beard  that slowly threatens to swallow his  face and the protagonist of monochrome  ax can barely move without stumbling the  red scarf boy struggles to clamber up  crates and swing from ropes he stiffly  jumps well short of his target and loses  his balance in precarious situations it  would be easy to pity his clumsiness  except that it's hard to have any  sympathy with the blinding frustration  that defines monochrome ah it took an  hour to admit that monochrome ax was not  ensnaring me as I expected the black and  white aesthetics paint a feeling of  hopelessness that immediately made me  question what made this world so Stark  an omnipresent corporation looms over  the rain-soaked city and without any  people around I felt lost and lonely  it's a great backdrop that tells a story  without any dialogue children's lives  are being threatened and so I had to  carry my younger brother to safety amid  the eerie desolation you run through the  cityscape without direction obstacles  continually obstruct your path so you  must use your wits to continue onward  puzzle design is one of monochrome of  strengths so you can do little more than  pull switches push boxes and perform a  modest jump there are variety of  situations that force you to take  careful stock of your surroundings to  figure out a solution you may have to  catch a swinging rope or douse a barrel  fire all while your brother clings to  your back  [Music]  [Music]  using a helpless family member to  strengthen one's emotional connection is  usually an easy way to invest me in a  journey but in monochrome a-- i only got  annoyed by my siblings uselessness  although you're introduced to your  brother by watching him fly a kite he's  no more than a limp dummy for the rest  of the game why can't he run alongside  you and you must place him in a  spotlight when you need to jump higher  than you could with him on your back  he's such a coward that you can't put  him anywhere else instead of feeling  protective I felt like I was lugging a  worthless lump the baffling relationship  your brother is just a start of  monochrome as problems figure out a way  to complete puzzles is often satisfying  but going through the required motions  is anything bucks long after you know  what you're supposed to do you'll still  be fighting the controls to get the darn  boy to do what he's told even simple  things are incredibly aggravating he may  not be able to jump onto certain ledges  for some reason or he'll hang onto a  switch even as you mash buttons nothing  feels right in monochrome oh and I could  never get over that disconnect there are  also a lot of inconsistencies that zap  away much of this simple joy of solving  a puzzle as nice as the visual design is  I often struggle to determine exactly  what I could interact with and I can't  count how many times I died from falling  too far even if it seemed like I should  be able to make it then there are little  problems such as loading screens  breaking up the flow of your adventuring  or the comical way that you die there's  so many times that I grown from  annoyance or laughs from absurdity that  I struggled to stay invested in what was  unfolding  monochromator nowt to be a massive  disappointment with a distinct art style  and clever puzzles it had so much  potential to be really special  but it's continually undermined by  technical problems so much show that I  struggled to even reach the end the  youthful protagonists of monochrome ah  is incredibly brave and filled with awe  inspiring love and patience but he's so  clumsy that I couldn't overlook his  negative aspects  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you  [Music]

